`ifndef HI3516AV100_CRG_RDL
`define HI3516AV100_CRG_RDL

regfile eCRG {
    name = "Clock and reset generator (CRG), Hi3516A V100 / Hi3516D V100";
    desc = "
    PERI_CRGn clock/reset registers at 0x20030000 (data sheet table 3-7, 36 registers: PERI_CRG0 .. PERI_CRG75 with gaps). Four PLLs (APLL, BPLL, VPLL, EPLL) fed by the 24 MHz XIN
    crystal. Reset values are the data sheet total reset values. Every module has a soft reset request bit (1 = reset, the reset is NOT released automatically, it stays
    until software writes 0) and a clock gate. The Hi3516A and the Hi3516D share this CRG; the Cortex-A7 uses the clock tree below.

    Clock facts for the bring-up code:
    - A7 (Cortex-A7): PERI_CRG12 cpu_sc_sel [9:8], reset 00 = APLL FOUTPOSTDIV (reset 24 MHz x 50 / 1 = 1200 MHz VCO, /2 = 600 MHz); 01 = 500 MHz, 10 = 400 MHz, 11 = BPLL FOUTPOSTDIV.
      The system controller powers up in slow mode (SYS_CTRL SC_CTRL reset 0x212, modectrl = 010), so the A7 runs from the 24 MHz crystal until software writes modectrl = 100 (normal), whatever cpu_sc_sel says.
      PERI_CRG10 cpuclk_skipcfg/cpuclk_loaden gives 1/32 step frequency scaling on top. APLL: PERI_CRG0/1; change it only in slow mode (the system controller mode), the PLL is
      stable 0.1 ms after a change, check PERI_CRG58 apll_lock. BPLL is powered down at reset. VPLL (1188 MHz VCO, 594/297/148.5/99/74.25 MHz) and EPLL (1000 MHz VCO, 500/250/125 MHz)
      are fixed in practice (spread spectrum in PERI_CRG67/68/70).
    - DDR: PERI_CRG12 ddr_sc_sel [5:4] (00 = 297 MHz, 10 = 250 MHz, 11 = 198 MHz; the vendor U-Boot reads it with DDR_MASK 0x30).
    - Bus: sysaxi = PERI_CRG12 sysaxi_sc_sel [3] (198 / 148.5 MHz); the system APB clock (timers, GPIO, WDG, I2C, UART parent) is sysaxi / 4 = 49.5 MHz (37.125 MHz). MDA0/MDA1 AXI: PERI_CRG12 [1:0] / [2].
    - UART: PERI_CRG57 uart_cksel [19]: 0 = APB (49.5 MHz), 1 = 6 MHz (reset value 1; vendor U-Boot clears it); gates bits 15..18. Timers: SP804 from 3 MHz or the APB clock (SYS_CTRL SC_CTRL timer selects).
    - Storage: SFC (NOR/NAND) PERI_CRG48 (24 / 75 / 125 MHz), NANDC PERI_CRG52 (24 / 198 MHz), SDIO0/1 PERI_CRG49 (50 / 100 / 25 / 75 MHz).
    - Ethernet (GSF/GMAC): PERI_CRG51 (resets bits 0/2, gates bits 1/3, RMII pad clock bit 4, external PHY clock 50/25 MHz bit 6), MAC interface mode PERI_CRG59.
    - USB 2.0: PERI_CRG46 at 0xB8. Reset deassert order (vendor U-Boot hiusb-3516a.c): usb_cken, MISC_CTRL30 setup, clear usbphy_req, PHY config via MISC + 0x80, clear usbphy_port0_treq,
      then usb_ctrl_utmi0_req / usb_ctrl_hub_req / usb_ahb_srst_req.
    - Video blocks: VI/MIPI PERI_CRG11, VOU PERI_CRG13, VEDU/AVC PERI_CRG16, VPSS PERI_CRG18, TDE PERI_CRG22, VGS PERI_CRG23, JPGE PERI_CRG24, MDU PERI_CRG26, IVE PERI_CRG27, AIO PERI_CRG35.

    Vendor Linux clock driver (crg-hi3516av100.c, `hisilicon,hi3516a-clock`, OpenIPC tree) uses: sysaxi_mux 0x30 bit 3, a7_mux 0x30 bits 9:8 (apll/500m/400m), snor_mux 0xC0 [3:2] and snand_mux 0xC0 [7:6], nand_mux 0xD0 bit 2, mmc0_mux 0xC4 [3:2], mmc1_mux 0xC4 [11:10], uart_mux 0xE4 bit 19, eth_phy_mux 0xCC bit 6; gates snor 0xC0 b1, snand 0xC0 b5, mmc0 0xC4 b1, mmc1 0xC4 b9, uart0..3 0xE4 b15..18, spi0/1 0xE4 b13/14, eth 0xCC b1, eth_macif 0xCC b3, dmac 0xD8 b5. Its reset controller is a no-op. Disagreements with the
    data sheet (data sheet followed): USB gates at 0xB4 b5/b0 (data sheet and vendor U-Boot: 0xB8); clk_nand gate at 0xD8 bit 1 (data sheet: 0xD0 bit 1, 0xD8 bit 1 is the eFUSE gate); the 50 MHz APB clock (49.5 MHz).

    Sources: HiSilicon English data sheet Hi3516A/Hi3516D Professional HD IP Camera SoC, Issue 08 (2016-10-28), chapter 3.1/3.2 (reset and clock; `hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt` lines 17960-20477).
    No Chinese original is available locally; the vendor U-Boot (arch-hi3516a/platform.h, board/hi3516a/board.c, arch/arm/cpu/hi3516a/lowlevel_init_svb.c, hiusb-3516a.c, higmacv300) and the vendor Linux clock driver
    were used to settle disputes. Checked 2026-11-09: names, offsets, bit ranges, accesses and resets of all 36 registers against the data sheet.
    Reserved ranges that the bit tables list as RW (PERI_CRG1-5, 8, 9, 65, 67, 68, 70, 75) are omitted; keep them at 0 (read-modify-write). PERI_CRG10 [0], PERI_CRG46 [6] and [3] and PERI_CRG67/68/70 [14] are reserved in the bit table but set in the total reset value; they are modelled as RO reserved_nz_* fields.
    Known data sheet errors: table 3-4 prints `cpu_sc_sel bit[8:7]` (register table: [9:8]); 3.2.5 `Precautions` says the A7 runs from the crystal after power on (register reset and figure 3-3: APLL); 3.2.4 example swaps postdiv1/postdiv2 compared with the reset values;
    PERI_CRG10 field names a7clk_* in the text vs cpuclk_* in the register; PERI_CRG16 `veudclk_loaden`; PERI_CRG18 `vpsclk_*` vs `vpssclk_*`; table 3-6 `tdeclk_skipcfg` for JPGE; PERI_CRG65 pwm_cksel0 vs pwm_cksel1; `ai0_cksel` for aio_cksel.
    ";

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG0 is APLL configuration register 0.

APLL (CPU PLL). XIN = 24 MHz. FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv (must be > 600 MHz and <= 2.4 GHz); FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2); FOUT1PH0 = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2 x 2), FOUT2 /4, FOUT3 /6, FOUT4 /8. Reset: postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 2 (this register), refdiv = 1, fbdiv = 50 (PERI_CRG1) -> VCO 1200 MHz, FOUTPOSTDIV 600 MHz. The vendor U-Boot (lowlevel_init_svb.c) decodes the CPU frequency with exactly this layout (PERI_CRG0 [30:28], [26:24]; PERI_CRG1 [17:12], [11:0]). Data sheet figure 3-3 gives 900 MHz as the maximum APLL FOUTPOSTDIV, the PERI_CRG10 example uses a 750 MHz CPU source, the vendor Linux clock driver stubs APLL as a fixed 850 MHz. DS section 3.2.4 says `postdiv2 is 2 and postdiv1 is 1` for its 600 MHz example while the reset values are postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 2 (same product).

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG0 (offset 0x0, printed page 3-12, `hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt` line 18467).";

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv2";
            desc = "Level-2 output divider of the APLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_postdiv2[30:28];

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv1";
            desc = "Level-1 output divider of the APLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2;
        } apll_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "apll_frac";
            desc = "Decimal divider of the APLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG0 @ 0x0;

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 1";
        desc = "PERI_CRG1 is APLL configuration register 1.

APLL: VCO power-down bits at reset: apll_foutvcopd = 1 and apll_fout4phasepd = 1 (those outputs are off), apll_postdivpd = 0 (FOUTPOSTDIV on, it feeds the A7). Reset VCO is 24 x 50 / 1 = 1200 MHz. The PLL is stable 0.1 ms after a change; check PERI_CRG58 apll_lock before switching the CPU to it.

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG1 (offset 0x4, printed page 3-12, `hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt` line 18495).";

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_bypass_enum {
            not_bypassed = 0 { name = "not bypassed"; desc = "not bypassed"; };
            bypassed = 1 { name = "bypassed"; desc = "bypassed"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_bypass";
            desc = "APLL clock frequency division bypass.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_bypass[26:26];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_dacpd_enum {
            normal = 0 { name = "normal operating mode"; desc = "normal operating mode"; };
            power_down = 1 { name = "power-down mode"; desc = "power-down mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_dacpd";
            desc = "APLL test signal control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_dacpd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_dacpd[25:25];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_dsmpd_enum {
            fractional = 0 { name = "decimal frequency-division mode"; desc = "decimal frequency-division mode"; };
            integer = 1 { name = "integral frequency-division mode"; desc = "integral frequency-division mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_dsmpd";
            desc = "APLL decimal division control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_dsmpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_dsmpd[24:24];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_pd_enum {
            normal = 0 { name = "normal operating mode"; desc = "normal operating mode"; };
            power_down = 1 { name = "power-down mode"; desc = "power-down mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_pd";
            desc = "APLL power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_pd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_pd[23:23];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_foutvcopd_enum {
            clock_on = 0 { name = "normal output clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            clock_off = 1 { name = "no output clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_foutvcopd";
            desc = "APLL VCO output power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_foutvcopd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_foutvcopd[22:22];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_postdivpd_enum {
            clock_on = 0 { name = "normal clock output"; desc = "normal clock output"; };
            clock_off = 1 { name = "no output clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_postdivpd";
            desc = "APLL POSTDIV output power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_postdivpd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_postdivpd[21:21];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_fout4phasepd_enum {
            clock_on = 0 { name = "normal output clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            clock_off = 1 { name = "no output clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_fout4phasepd";
            desc = "APLL FOUT output power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_fout4phasepd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_fout4phasepd[20:20];

        field {
            name = "apll_refdiv";
            desc = "Frequency divider of the APLL reference clock.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_refdiv[17:12];

        field {
            name = "apll_fbdiv";
            desc = "Integral frequency multiplier of the APLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x32;
        } apll_fbdiv[11:0];
    } PERI_CRG1 @ 0x4;

    reg {
        name = "BPLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG2 is BPLL configuration register 0.

BPLL: powered down at reset (see PERI_CRG3). Optional A7 source (PERI_CRG12 cpu_sc_sel = 3 selects BPLL_FOUTPOSTDIV) and AIO MCLK source (PERI_CRG35 aio_cksel = 1 selects BPLL_FOUTVCO).

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG2 (offset 0x8, printed page 3-14, `hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt` line 18566).";

        field {
            name = "bpll_postdiv2";
            desc = "Level-2 output divider of the BPLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } bpll_postdiv2[30:28];

        field {
            name = "bpll_postdiv1";
            desc = "Level-1 output divider of the BPLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x3;
        } bpll_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "bpll_frac";
            desc = "Decimal divider of the BPLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } bpll_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG2 @ 0x8;

    reg {
        name = "BPLL configuration register 1";
        desc = "PERI_CRG3 is BPLL configuration register 1.

BPLL reset values: bpll_pd = 1, bpll_foutvcopd = 1, bpll_postdivpd = 1, bpll_fout4phasepd = 1 (data sheet 3.2.3: `the BPLL is powered down by default`); programmed values would give VCO 24 x 54 / 1 = 1296 MHz and POSTDIV (/3) 432 MHz.

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG3 (offset 0xC, printed page 3-14, `hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt` line 18595).";

        enum PERI_CRG3_bpll_bypass_enum {
            not_bypassed = 0 { name = "not bypassed"; desc = "not bypassed"; };
            bypassed = 1 { name = "bypassed"; desc = "bypassed"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "bpll_bypass";
            desc = "BPLL clock frequency division bypass.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_bpll_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } bpll_bypass[26:26];

        enum PERI_CRG3_bpll_dacpd_enum {
            normal = 0 { name = "normal operating mode"; desc = "normal operating mode"; };
            power_down = 1 { name = "power-down mode"; desc = "power-down mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "bpll_dacpd";
            desc = "BPLL test signal control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_bpll_dacpd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } bpll_dacpd[25:25];

        enum PERI_CRG3_bpll_dsmpd_enum {
            fractional = 0 { name = "decimal frequency-division mode"; desc = "decimal frequency-division mode"; };
            integer = 1 { name = "integral frequency-division mode"; desc = "integral frequency-division mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "bpll_dsmpd";
            desc = "BPLL decimal division control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_bpll_dsmpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } bpll_dsmpd[24:24];

        enum PERI_CRG3_bpll_pd_enum {
            normal = 0 { name = "normal operating mode"; desc = "normal operating mode"; };
            power_down = 1 { name = "power-down mode"; desc = "power-down mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "bpll_pd";
            desc = "BPLL power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_bpll_pd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } bpll_pd[23:23];

        enum PERI_CRG3_bpll_foutvcopd_enum {
            clock_on = 0 { name = "normal output clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            clock_off = 1 { name = "no output clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "bpll_foutvcopd";
            desc = "BPLL VCO output power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_bpll_foutvcopd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } bpll_foutvcopd[22:22];

        enum PERI_CRG3_bpll_postdivpd_enum {
            clock_on = 0 { name = "normal output clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            clock_off = 1 { name = "no output clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "bpll_postdivpd";
            desc = "BPLL POSTDIV output power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_bpll_postdivpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } bpll_postdivpd[21:21];

        enum PERI_CRG3_bpll_fout4phasepd_enum {
            clock_on = 0 { name = "normal output clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            clock_off = 1 { name = "no output clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "bpll_fout4phasepd";
            desc = "BPLL FOUT output power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_bpll_fout4phasepd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } bpll_fout4phasepd[20:20];

        field {
            name = "bpll_refdiv";
            desc = "Frequency divider of the BPLL reference clock.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } bpll_refdiv[17:12];

        field {
            name = "bpll_fbdiv";
            desc = "Integral frequency multiplier of the BPLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x36;
        } bpll_fbdiv[11:0];
    } PERI_CRG3 @ 0xC;

    reg {
        name = "VPLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG4 is VPLL configuration register 0.

VPLL: reset VCO = 24 x 99 / 2 = 1188 MHz, FOUTPOSTDIV (/2) = 594 MHz, FOUT1PH0 297 MHz, FOUT2 148.5 MHz, FOUT3 99 MHz, FOUT4 74.25 MHz (data sheet figure 3-3; the vendor Linux driver names them 594m, 297m, 148.5m, 99m, 74.25m). Source of the video clocks (VI, VO, VPSS, AVC/VEDU, DDR and bus 297/198/148.5/99 MHz).

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG4 (offset 0x10, printed page 3-16, `hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt` line 18665).";

        field {
            name = "vpll_postdiv2";
            desc = "Level-2 output divider of VPLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } vpll_postdiv2[30:28];

        field {
            name = "vpll_postdiv1";
            desc = "Level-1 output divider of VPLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2;
        } vpll_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "vpll_frac";
            desc = "Decimal divider of VPLL.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG4 @ 0x10;

    reg {
        name = "VPLL configuration register 1";
        desc = "PERI_CRG5 is VPLL configuration register 1.

VPLL reset VCO: 24 x 99 / 2 = 1188 MHz. VPLL runs from reset (all power-down bits 0).

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG5 (offset 0x14, printed page 3-16, `hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt` line 18694).";

        enum PERI_CRG5_vpll_bypass_enum {
            not_bypassed = 0 { name = "not bypassed"; desc = "not bypassed"; };
            bypassed = 1 { name = "bypassed"; desc = "bypassed"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "vpll_bypass";
            desc = "VPLL clock frequency division bypass.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG5_vpll_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll_bypass[26:26];

        enum PERI_CRG5_vpll_dacpd_enum {
            normal = 0 { name = "normal operating mode"; desc = "normal operating mode"; };
            power_down = 1 { name = "power-down mode"; desc = "power-down mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "vpll_dacpd";
            desc = "VPLL test signal control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG5_vpll_dacpd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll_dacpd[25:25];

        enum PERI_CRG5_vpll_dsmpd_enum {
            fractional = 0 { name = "decimal frequency-division mode"; desc = "decimal frequency-division mode"; };
            integer = 1 { name = "integral frequency-division mode"; desc = "integral frequency-division mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "vpll_dsmpd";
            desc = "VPLL decimal division control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG5_vpll_dsmpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } vpll_dsmpd[24:24];

        enum PERI_CRG5_vpll_pd_enum {
            normal = 0 { name = "normal operating mode"; desc = "normal operating mode"; };
            power_down = 1 { name = "power-down mode"; desc = "power-down mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "vpll_pd";
            desc = "VPLL power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG5_vpll_pd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll_pd[23:23];

        enum PERI_CRG5_vpll_foutvcopd_enum {
            clock_on = 0 { name = "normal output clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            clock_off = 1 { name = "no output clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "vpll_foutvcopd";
            desc = "VPLL VCO output power-down control.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG5_vpll_foutvcopd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll_foutvcopd[22:22];

        enum PERI_CRG5_vpll_postdivpd_enum {
            clock_on = 0 { name = "normal output clock"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            clock_off = 1 { name = "no output clock"; desc = "no output clock"; };
