    reg {
        name = "SoC clock selection register";
        desc = "PERI_CRG12 is an SoC clock selection register.

SoC clock selection. A7: cpu_sc_sel [9:8] (reset 00 = APLL_FOUTPOSTDIV = 600 MHz at reset); the vendor Linux clock driver (crg-hi3516av100.c a7_mux, offset 0x30 bits 9:8, table {apll 0, 500m 1, 400m 2}) and the vendor U-Boot (lowlevel_init_svb.c CPU_MASK 0x300) agree. DS section 3.2.5 table 3-4 prints `bit[8:7]` for cpu_sc_sel, the register table [9:8] is right. DS 3.2.5 `Precautions` says the A7 runs from the crystal after power on while this register resets to cpu_sc_sel = 00 (APLL_FOUTPOSTDIV); both are right: the system controller powers up in slow mode (SYS_CTRL SC_CTRL total reset 0x212 = modectrl 010 `slow`, modestatus 0x2; data sheet lines 20808, 20886), in which the ARM subsystem is clocked from the 24 MHz crystal regardless of this mux, and only after software writes modectrl = 100 (normal) does cpu_sc_sel choose the PLL clock (600 MHz APLL at reset). The slow/normal switch is a SYS_CTRL mode, not a CRG mux. DDR: ddr_sc_sel [5:4] (vendor U-Boot DDR_MASK 0x30; reset 297 MHz). Bus: sysaxi_sc_sel [3] (vendor Linux sysaxi_mux 0x30 bit 3: 198m / 148.5m) -> system APB clock = sysaxi / 4 = 49.5 MHz (37.125 MHz when 148.5 MHz is selected); the vendor Linux driver calls the APB clock `50 MHz` and uses a fixed 50m parent for the UART/DMAC gates. The data sheet describes mda_sc_sel [19:12] and bus_sc_sel [3:0] as single fields containing several sub-selectors; this file splits them into the individual 2/1-bit selectors (avc/vgs/vpss/vedu_sc_sel, sysaxi/mda1axi/mda0axi_sc_sel) so that every selector has its own enum.

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG12 (offset 0x30, printed page 3-22, `hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt` line 18999).";

