USB 2.0 host/device clock and soft reset control. The vendor U-Boot USB driver (hiusb-3516a.c) uses this register at offset 0xB8 as the data sheet does; the vendor Linux clock driver crg-hi3516av100.c uses offset 0xB4 (bits 5 and 0, gate flag SET_TO_DISABLE) for the same bits, which is a driver bug (0xB4 is not a register in this data sheet). Vendor U-Boot reset deassert order: set usb_cken (bit 7), wait 100 us; configure the controller in MISC_CTRL30 (misc + 0x78); clear usbphy_req (bit 1), wait 100 us; program the PHY through the undocumented MISC + 0x80 port (0xc06/0xc26, 0x1c00/0x1c20, 0x0c09/0x0c29, 0x1a0a/0x1a2a, with 5 ms delays); clear usbphy_port0_treq (bit 2), wait 300 us; clear usb_ctrl_utmi0_req (bit 5), usb_ctrl_hub_req (bit 4) and usb_ahb_srst_req (bit 0), wait 200 us; finally MISC + 0x80 = 0xa then 0x092a. Reset 0xFF: all resets asserted, PHY reference clock gate on.

