    reg {
        name = "GMAC interface control register";
        desc = "PERI_CRG59 is a GMAC interface control register.

GMAC interface (MACIF) control: PHY interface mode, speed, duplex, link, TX enable. Vendor U-Boot higmacv300 uses this register at CRG + 0xEC (REG_ETH_MAC_IF) for the MAC interface mode, matches. Reset 0x3F: RGMII, full duplex, TX config on, link up, 100 Mbit/s, 10/100 port. The vendor U-Boot (higmacv300/higmac.h, higmac.c calculate_port_mode) writes exactly these encodings to this register: 10M MII 0x1D, 100M MII 0x1F, 10M RGMII 0x3D, 100M RGMII 0x3F, 1000M RGMII 0x3C (mac_speed 0, port_select 0), 10M RMII 0x9D, 100M RMII 0x9F; half duplex clears bit 4. All agree with the fields below.

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG59 (offset 0xEC, printed page 3-44, `hi3516av100--Hi3516A-Hi3516D-Datasheet.txt` line 20189).";

        enum PERI_CRG59_loopback_mode_enum {
            disabled = 0 { name = "disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            enabled = 1 { name = "enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "loopback_mode";
            desc = "Loopback mode enable.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG59_loopback_mode_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
